// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -use-structuring-pass -emit-cir -emit-llvm -output %t >> /dev/null 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=CIR %s --input-file %t.cir
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=LL %s --input-file %t.ll

// Two grounded vocabularies are exercised here:
//
//   1. Stock Ghidra 12.0.4 AArch64 SLEIGH CALLOTHER userops:
//        DataMemoryBarrier, DataSynchronizationBarrier,
//        InstructionSynchronizationBarrier, ClearExclusiveLocal,
//        LOAcquire, LORelease, SpeculationBarrier
//      (Ghidra/Processors/AARCH64/data/languages/AARCH64instructions.sinc)
//
//   2. LLVM compiler-rt AArch64 outline-atomic helper symbols:
//        __aarch64_<base><size><ordering>
//      (compiler-rt/lib/builtins/aarch64/lse.S)
//      Real binaries built with -moutline-atomics call these as ordinary
//      external functions; this fixture confirms the normalizer maps the
//      symbol name to the C11 atomic canonical even when the upstream
//      pipeline surfaces it as an intrinsic CALLOTHER.

